  "question": {
    "html": "<p>A variable resistor with a resistance range of 0 to 6.0 kΩ is connected in series with two resistors of fixed value 6.0 kΩ. The cell in the circuit has an emf of 18 V and a negligible internal resistance.</p>\n<p><figure data-asset-id=\"fig_01\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 1\" src=\"asset:fig_01\"/></figure></p>\n<p>What is the maximum range of potential difference that can be observed between X and Y? <br/><br/></p>\n<p>[1]</p>\n<ol class=\"mcq-options\"><li data-label=\"A\">0 to 12 V</li><li data-label=\"B\">6.0 V to 9.0 V</li><li data-label=\"C\">9.0 V to 12 V</li><li data-label=\"D\">9.0 V to 18 V</li></ol>"
  },
